<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila succini Turing wavenumber at 2.8 µm (44 Ma, detail scale s0) (Drosophila succini)",
        "Drosophila succini Turing wavenumber at 2.8 µm (44 Ma, detail scale s0) faithfully reproduces Drosophila succini morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3172_drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila succini specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3172_drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila succini" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 10.1163/187631265X00018 is a resolvable DOI.",
        "does_not_claim: That the GIF's spot field is a photograph of Drosophila succini.",
        "does_not_claim: That the full Fourier spectrum of the nonlinear PDE matches linear theory (it does not, outside the Turing band).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Berryi wavelength 2.382 µm by transferring the registry ratio 98.43/114 onto this detail scale.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian, sigma(k), k_c = argmax sigma, D_u solved so lambda = 2.759e-06 m at r = 18.72.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Stem r = 8.40 below onset and equal-diffusivity ablation have sigma_max < 0.",
        "reported_in_source: Grimaldi 1987: Dominican amber drosophilids, the chronoseries context for the 19 Ma successor.",
        "reported_in_source: Hennig 1965: Drosophila succini is a Baltic amber acalyptrate, volume 145.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: du/dt = a - u + u^2 v and dv/dt = b - u^2 v, plus diffusion.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system selects a critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: Kondo & Miura 2010 is a framework paper, not a datum for this fossil.",
        "transfer_boundary: No published measurement of a 2.8 µm pigment wavelength in the Hennig holotype.",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery card is a synthetic spiral, not an amber photomicrograph." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila succini (Eocene Baltic Amber Stem Drosophilid)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-succini-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3172_drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0.lean; output: docs/media/drosophila_succini_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila succini; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion system selects a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: du/dt = a - u + u^2 v and dv/dt = b - u^2 v, plus diffusion. | Hennig 1965: Drosophila succini is a Baltic amber acalyptrate, volume 145. | Grimaldi 1987: Dominican amber drosophilids, the chronoseries context for the 19 Ma successor.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian, sigma(k), k_c = argmax sigma, D_u solved so lambda = 2.759e-06 m at r = 18.72. | Stem r = 8.40 below onset and equal-diffusivity ablation have sigma_max < 0. | Berryi wavelength 2.382 µm by transferring the registry ratio 98.43/114 onto this detail scale.; transfer_boundary: No published measurement of a 2.8 µm pigment wavelength in the Hennig holotype. | Kondo & Miura 2010 is a framework paper, not a datum for this fossil. | The gallery card is a synthetic spiral, not an amber photomicrograph.; does_not_claim: That the GIF's spot field is a photograph of Drosophila succini. | That the full Fourier spectrum of the nonlinear PDE matches linear theory (it does not, outside the Turing band). | That 10.1163/187631265X00018 is a resolvable DOI.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
